Action Due — 2026-09-28', 'assignment-desk-xlsm-v1:dlpc:Assignment Desk:0004', '{"Workbook row": 4, "Candidate / Slug": "TOPIC UPDATE: UHS HVAC Systems Progress", "Coverage Area": "La Porte City / Dysart", "Category": "Education", "Source / Link": "https://www.union.k12.ia.us/district/board-of-education/ | Sept. 21 minutes: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QepRO3BtJansCdEZz_pBzXu_zoRPL1Xi/view", "Date / Event Date": "46286.0", "Editorial Horizon": "This Week", "Dan Decision": "Do", "Priority": "High", "Status": "Reporting hold — November16 outcome not yet posted", "Next Action": "Cover the Nov. 16 board outcome, not the agenda as a decision. If approved, verify the Dec. 16 hearing notices for high-school HVAC/fire alarm, roofing and middle/elementary HVAC/restroom work. Resolve the newsletter''s Feb. 10 versus official Feb. 16 bond-date conflict before using that date.", "Action Due": "46293.0", "New Since Last Run": "Nov. 8: Fall 2026 newsletter confirms the $10.5 million SAVE-backed program, December HVAC bidding and May 2027 work start. Its Feb. 10 approval date conflicts with the official Feb. 16 record.\nNov. 13: Nov. 16 agenda proposes scheduling three Dec. 16 public hearings and discusses early retirement. No action has occurred yet.", "Developing?": "No", "Follow-up Owed?": "No", "Graphic Needed?": "No", "Graphic Type": "None", "Script / Treatment Notes": "No generic meeting recap; pursue only material decisions affecting families, taxes, facilities or services.", "Jack Notes": "Sept. 21 minutes posted Sept. 25: board voted 6-0 for a professional-services agreement with Eocene Environmental Group, but no scope, price or rationale appears in minutes. It also voted 6-0 to request a $227,867.97 modified supplemental amount from the School Budget Review Committee for the 2025-26 special-education deficit; this is a request, not confirmed state approval or a new levy. The six preceding meetings (May 18, June 3, June 18, July 1, July 22, Aug. 17) contain no further substantive discussion of Eocene or this deficit request. Sept. 21 minutes also approve an ongoing Hawkeye Community College student-field-experience agreement, 2026-27 legal-services engagement, Academic Decathlon national trip and Craft family gift for UHS upper gym, with few terms. Do not draft generic recap or mark Do without Dan’s decision.\nOct.4 All Mail reconciliation: Sept.29 John Howard on-record reply supports asbestos screening/Ecocene and SAVE funding already reflected in draft. Sept.30 exchange was explicitly off-record: internal background only, not a public citation or quote.\nNov. 8 10 p.m. thorough run: existing NRCS story 930ac926-fb0c-441f-b62a-ee13c103a1b3 was found Active, preventing duplicate coverage. Added the public Fall 2026 newsletter as a source and saved an internal facts note. Public output was not changed or queued because the newsletter''s Feb. 10 approval date conflicts with the district''s official Feb. 16 board/public-notice record.\nNov. 13 source: Union Nov. 16 board agenda delivered by Stephanie Seuser, Gmail 1a1d66c5a67bd514. Existing active story/public article found; no duplicate proposed. Bus specifications and transportation pay rates are agenda items; no routes/stops/schedules used.\nNov18 targeted official board page still lists November16 Agenda only, no minutes. Do not convert proposed December hearings into approved actions. Existing live story preserved.", "Action Due (local)": "2026-09-28", "Date / Event Date (local)": "2026-09-21"}', 'legacy_do', '') on conflict (legacy_key) do nothing;
