Action Due — 2026-11-15', 'assignment-desk-xlsm-v1:dlpc:Assignment Desk:0006', '{"Workbook row": 6, "Candidate / Slug": "2026 general election: local voting guide", "Coverage Area": "La Porte City / Dysart", "Category": "Elections", "Source / Link": "Tama: https://www.tamacounty.iowa.gov/elections/info/2026_general_election_2026_11_03/ | Black Hawk: https://blackhawkcountyelections.iowa.gov/elections/info/2026_general_election_2026_11_03/ | Iowa judicial retention: https://www.iowacourts.gov/newsroom/news-releases/information-about-iowas-2026-judicial-retention-elections", "Date / Event Date": "46329.0", "Editorial Horizon": "Upcoming", "Dan Decision": "Do", "Priority": "Normal", "Status": "Retired — October production queue", "Next Action": "Dan directed removal of outdated October work Nov.11. No further action on this old production assignment; retain source/story history. Reopen only for a genuinely new verified assignment. Existing NRCS stories and published outputs were not deleted or altered.", "Action Due": "46341.0", "Repeat Strategy": "Refresh as county information is posted; time around voting deadlines.", "New Since Last Run": "Nov. 7: Tama County officially scheduled its Nov. 10 canvass; exact local results remain unofficial until canvass.", "Developing?": "No", "Follow-up Owed?": "No", "Graphic Needed?": "No", "Graphic Type": "None", "Script / Treatment Notes": "Practical voting information, not a generic horse-race story. Identify county-specific details and link official lookup tools.", "Jack Notes": "Black Hawk County: Nov. 3 polls 7 a.m.–8 p.m.; Oct. 14 absentee voting begins; Oct. 19 at 5 p.m. registration and mailed-ballot request deadlines; Nov. 2 at 4:30 p.m. in-person absentee ends; ballot returned by 8 p.m. Nov. 3. Precinct page lists Union High School, 200 Adams St., for La Porte City/Big Creek/Spring Creek; county cautions location can vary by election, so confirm election page or voter lookup. La Porte City sample ballot Style 7 is posted. Tama County confirms Dysart Community Building, 418 Main St. No NRCS election result.\nSept.30 verification advance: Tama now posts an 88-page Nov.3 sample ballot, including Dysart City on PDF pages 11–12 (Seq.0006). Reverse includes Public Measure TX reducing county supervisors from five to three and the statewide income-tax supermajority constitutional amendment. This is verified ballot content, not a new Sept.30 board action. NRCS voting guide v7 still says Tama sample ballots will be added later. Sample: https://www.tamacounty.iowa.gov/files/sample_ballots/1202_sample_ballot_57956.pdf. Update existing voting guide when Dan authorizes, including precinct-specific candidate details; do not create duplicate election coverage. Verify implementation timing of TX separately.\nOct.12 advance: official Iowa Judicial Branch retention-election release added. Statewide counts do not mean every voter sees every trial judge; district/sample-ballot matching remains required.\nOct.23 NRCS handoff: Web Copy v3 headline is ''Election Day is November 3; early voting is underway.'' It removes elapsed deadlines as upcoming, retains county-specific current service details and flags Tama hours for confirmation. Existing published output was not replaced.\nNov.11, 2026 Newsroom Jack: Retired old assignment per Dan; not a claim of completed reporting or a cancellation of the underlying policy/service. Dan Decision preserved.", "Action Due (local)": "2026-11-15", "Date / Event Date (local)": "2026-11-03"}', 'legacy_do', '') on conflict (legacy_key) do nothing;
