Action Due — 2026-10-04', 'assignment-desk-xlsm-v1:dlpc:Assignment Desk:0020', '{"Workbook row": 20, "Candidate / Slug": "Upstream runoff: current flood risk near Dysart and La Porte City", "Coverage Area": "La Porte City / Dysart", "Category": "Alert / Weather", "Source / Link": "https://forecast.weather.gov/wwamap/wwatxtget.php?cwa=DMX&wwa=flood+watch", "Date / Event Date": "46295.0", "Editorial Horizon": "Immediate", "Dan Decision": "too late", "Decision Reason": "Can you find the likelyhood that LPC/Dysart will ACTUALLY be impacted? Rainfaill has subsided and weather is looking dry through the week, so additional flooding would have to come from upstream.", "Priority": "Lead", "Status": "Retired — October production queue", "Next Action": "Dan directed removal of outdated October work Nov.11. No further action on this old production assignment; retain source/story history. Reopen only for a genuinely new verified assignment. Existing NRCS stories and published outputs were not deleted or altered.", "Action Due": "46299.0", "Repeat Strategy": "On NWS updates until expiry; no repeat without changed information.", "New Since Last Run": "Oct.9 NWS warning text retrieved; no LPC/Dysart warning in that text. Live Wolf Creek levels not retrieved. Do not reuse Oct.4 levels as current.", "Developing?": "Yes", "Follow-up Owed?": "No", "Graphic Needed?": "No", "Graphic Type": "Alert", "Script / Treatment Notes": "Alert/service treatment; no automatic publication.", "Jack Notes": "NWS DMX Sept.30 1:42 a.m. CDT continuation includes Black Hawk and Tama; coded expiry Oct.2 1 a.m. CDT. Excessive-rainfall flooding possible. Watch is not a flood warning or proof of flooding in either town. Treat as weather/alert workflow, not a manufactured news story.\nNRCS: Sept.30 DLPC all-lifecycle story inventory checked; no matching new story found.\nOct.4 risk check: NWS DMX flood-watch page has no active text. Flood-warning bulletin lists Hudson reach to Waterloo and Iowa River near Tama, not Wolf Creek/LPC/Dysart. Dry local weather alone cannot rule out delayed upstream runoff. Retrieved Dysart USGS reading is dated Sept.2 and unusable as current evidence; LPC site05464250 has no continuous data. NOAA hydrographs did not expose live levels in retrieval. No defensible local probability or all-clear yet. Sources: https://forecast.weather.gov/wwamap/wwatxtget.php?cwa=DMX&wwa=flood+warning ; https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/dysi4 ; https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/aloi4 .\nOct.4 live browser evidence supersedes earlier retrieval limitation: DYSI4 6.90ft at9:15CDT, below action10/minor12. LAPI4 811.77ft NAVD88 at9:30, below MainStreet impact814. Both Wolf Creek pages show no official forecast and no active area alerts. ALOI4 10.47ft at9:00, below minor13; forecast issued8:56 has next maximum10.3 then decline. Banner warning concerns Black Hawk Creek at Hudson, not Cedar River at Waterloo. Supports monitoring rather than imminent town flooding; local ponding/road impacts not established. Gauge datums differ. https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/dysi4#hg=official ; https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/LAPI4#hg=official ; https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/aloi4#hg=official .\nNov.11, 2026 Newsroom Jack: Retired old assignment per Dan; not a claim of completed reporting or a cancellation of the underlying policy/service. Dan Decision preserved.", "Action Due (local)": "2026-10-04", "Date / Event Date (local)": "2026-09-30"}', 'skip', 'Can you find the likelyhood that LPC/Dysart will ACTUALLY be impacted? Rainfaill has subsided and weather is looking dry through the week, so additional flooding would have to come from upstream.') on conflict (legacy_key) do nothing;
