eatment Notes": "Governance/service explainer only after comparing the current and proposed bylaws; do not imply tax, dispatch or response-time changes without evidence.", "Jack Notes": "Oct.13 agenda sets first public reading at 6:30 p.m., includes funding discussion and scheduling a second reading. Draft gives each participating member one vote, requires a representative and alternate, and sets 51% quorum; Executive Board list names Billie Van Egmond for Dysart. Current bylaws were not publicly located, so the amendment delta remains unknown.\nCurrent board roster: Billie Van Egmond, Dysart, alternate Tim Brown; Jane Whittlesey, La Porte City, alternate Jasmine Gaston. Representation is verified; no tax, dispatch or response-time consequence is established.\nOct.25 Jack: Oct.13 minutes establish second public reading Nov.2 at 6:30 p.m., Dysart Ambulance Service Building, 424 Main St. First valid reading Oct.13 after correcting earlier process. Draft has membership/quorum/voting provisions; adopted baseline not located, so changes cannot yet be identified. LPC absent Oct.13; Dysart voted aye. https://www.tamacounty.iowa.gov/files/meetings/2026-10-13_minutes_2153.pdf | https://www.tamacounty.iowa.gov/files/911/tama_county_joint_911_service_board_bylaws_draft_24609.pdf\nNov.11, 2026 Newsroom Jack: Retired old assignment per Dan; not a claim of completed reporting or a cancellation of the underlying policy/service. Dan Decision preserved.", "Action Due (local)": "2026-11-01", "Date / Event Date (local)": "2026-10-13"}', 'need_more_info', '') on conflict (legacy_key) do nothing;
